course: dictionary
lesson: 9989
title: Technology: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Technology changes fast; many jobs today, like app developer or social media manager, did not exist 30 years ago.» The clues are fast change and new jobs, so technology must mean the machines, tools and ways of doing things that people make with science and knowledge.
explain: Technology can also mean one particular kind of tool or method. «A technology» is a countable noun, so you can have one technology or many technologies. «Solar technology» means tools that use the power of the Sun.
explain: Look at the words next to it. «Information technology» and «digital technology» are phrases about computers and the internet. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: «Many future jobs will be about making technology fair and safe for people» still makes sense if you think of machines and computers.
fact: Technology means the use of science and knowledge to make useful tools, machines and ways of doing things.
fact: In everyday life, technology often means computers, phones, screens and the internet.
fact: «Technology» is uncountable when you talk about it in general, but «a technology» means one kind, and the plural is «technologies».
fact: Useful phrases: «modern technology», «new technology», «information technology (IT)» and «digital technology».
fact: In Design and Technology (D&T) lessons, pupils design, build and code things to solve problems.
exercise: «Technology changes fast; many jobs today did not exist 30 years ago.» What does technology mean here? | *Machines, tools and ways of doing things made with science | People who play games online | Old books kept in a library | A type of weather
exercise: Which phrase is about computers and the internet? | Long walk home | Ancient technology | *Digital technology | Solar sunshine
exercise: Mia says, «I need a technology for my science project.» What does a technology mean here? | A sad feeling about the future | Every machine in the world all together | *One particular kind of tool or method, like solar technology | The sound a phone makes
test: «Lots of older people use technology well; a rule about everyone of one age is a stereotype.» What does stereotype mean? | *A fixed, unfair idea about a whole group of people | A happy song | A new kind of phone | A very old machine
test: Which word is the plural of «a technology», meaning more than one kind of tool or method? | *technologies | technologist | technology | techies
exam: «Many future jobs will be about making technology fair and safe for people; maths, science, writing and kindness all help.» According to the sentence, what helps with these jobs? | *Maths, science, writing and kindness | Only sport and singing | Cooking and driving lessons | Nothing, because jobs never change
